        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This Memorandum of Understanding is entered into between the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, acting through the Human Resources Division, and the Massachusetts Organization of State Engineers and Scientists, Unit 9. This Memorandum of Understanding reflects a clarification of Articles 12 and 24A of the collective bargaining agreement concerning merit based pay for performance. It shall be agreed that:",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                226,
                1076,
                398
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    226.0
                ],
                [
                    1076.0,
                    226.0
                ],
                [
                    1076.0,
                    398.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    398.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. All EPRS evaluations shall be based on a “below”, “meets”, “exceeds” system. Such system shall commence on July 1, 2000.",
            "block_bbox": [
                141,
                424,
                1075,
                482
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    141.0,
                    424.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    424.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    482.0
                ],
                [
                    141.0,
                    482.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. Disciplinary actions impacting on an employee's \"ability to perform his/her normal duties\" shall be considered for the purpose of a final overall rating on the performance review.",
            "block_bbox": [
                138,
                509,
                1071,
                597
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    138.0,
                    509.0
                ],
                [
                    1071.0,
                    509.0
                ],
                [
                    1071.0,
                    597.0
                ],
                [
                    138.0,
                    597.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. Disciplinary actions not impacting on an employee's \"ability to perform his/her duties\" shall not have a greater impact than other areas of the employee's evaluation for the purpose of any rating.",
            "block_bbox": [
                138,
                622,
                1075,
                710
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    138.0,
                    622.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    622.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    710.0
                ],
                [
                    138.0,
                    710.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. A. Any appeal of a final “unsatisfactory” or “below” rating shall be initiated at a Merit\nArbitration Panel as designated below.",
            "block_bbox": [
                140,
                736,
                1069,
                820
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    140.0,
                    736.0
                ],
                [
                    1069.0,
                    736.0
                ],
                [
                    1069.0,
                    820.0
                ],
                [
                    140.0,
                    820.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "B. Said appeal shall be filed within 21 calendar days with the Human Resources Division.",
            "block_bbox": [
                174,
                849,
                1071,
                905
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    174.0,
                    849.0
                ],
                [
                    1071.0,
                    849.0
                ],
                [
                    1071.0,
                    905.0
                ],
                [
                    174.0,
                    905.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C. Only employees receiving a rating of “unsatisfactory” or “below” shall be able to appeal the rating.",
            "block_bbox": [
                176,
                935,
                1068,
                993
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    176.0,
                    935.0
                ],
                [
                    1068.0,
                    935.0
                ],
                [
                    1068.0,
                    993.0
                ],
                [
                    176.0,
                    993.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "D. The appeal shall be considered by a Merit Arbitration Panel consisting of one person designated by the Personnel Administrator, one person designated by the President of MOSES and one person designated by the Chairperson of the Board of Conciliation and Arbitration who shall be assigned on a rotating basis.",
            "block_bbox": [
                176,
                1019,
                1073,
                1135
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    176.0,
                    1019.0
                ],
                [
                    1073.0,
                    1019.0
                ],
                [
                    1073.0,
                    1135.0
                ],
                [
                    176.0,
                    1135.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "E. The standard of review to be applied by the panel shall be solely limited to whether or not the final performance of rating of “unsatisfactory” or “below” was justified.",
            "block_bbox": [
                177,
                1160,
                1072,
                1247
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    177.0,
                    1160.0
                ],
                [
                    1072.0,
                    1160.0
                ],
                [
                    1072.0,
                    1247.0
                ],
                [
                    177.0,
                    1247.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "F. The decision of the Merit Arbitration Panel shall be final and binding and any employee having an “unsatisfactory” or “below” rating overturned shall be made whole in as prompt a manner as possible. Any costs associated with this process will be borne equally by the parties.",
            "block_bbox": [
                176,
                1273,
                1079,
                1390
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11,
